    "applicability": {
      "scope": "Select and diagnose Ascend parallel strategies and their activation/overlap, with a separately bounded native multi-rank HCCL AllReduce dispatch and correctness procedure.",
      "input_contract": "Installed collective/runtime builds, rank/device map and topology, workload/strategy settings, count/dtype/reduction, effective dispatch, per-rank outputs and completed-collective/application timing evidence.",
      "produced_artifact": "A topology- and workload-qualified strategy/dispatch diagnosis, activation and correctness checks, stage-cost attribution and a target-validation proposal; isolated test completion is not a service result.",
      "failure_modes": "Requested parallel settings can silently fall back; stale local-head/chunk/shard parameters can disable a path, and changed topology/card count can confound strategy comparisons."
    },
    "state": "candidate",
    "limitations": [
      "Source-derived candidate; no local efficacy validation.",
      "Only the declared communication-test and native HCCL source slices are normalized; inherited strategy guidance and its source identities remain unchanged.",
      "Wrapper inspection does not qualify native HCCL/TorchNPU implementations, transport algorithms, numerical correctness, backend compatibility or measured gains.",
      "Native source coverage is one selected multi-rank AICPU mesh one-shot AllReduce path at the HCCL pin; legacy device routes, other engines/collectives and HCOMM transport/runtime implementations are not qualified.",
      "Inspected upstream tests use simulated task-graph semantics; neither those tests nor native numerical, memory, bandwidth, model-quality or service experiments were run.",
      "Checkout-only local skill; no automatic execution or promotion.",
      "Only declared references are required; other cross-skill links are navigation.",
